'''Llanquihue Lake'''<ref>{{Cite web |title=Llanquihue Lake |url=https://www.chile.travel/en/where-to-go/destination/llanquihue-lake/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230519004459/https://www.chile.travel/en/where-to-go/destination/llanquihue-lake/ |archive-date=May 19, 2023 |access-date=May 18, 2023 |website=chile.travel |publisher=[[Ministry of Economy, Development and Tourism (Chile)|Ministry of Economy, Development, and Tourism]]}}</ref> is the second-largest [[lake]] in [[Chile]] with an area of about {{convert|871|km2|sqmi|abbr=on}}, after [[Lake General Carrera]] which is shared with [[Argentina]]. It is situated in the southern [[Los Lagos Region]] in the [[Llanquihue Province|Llanquihue]] and [[Osorno Province|Osorno]] provinces. The lake's fan-like form was created by successive [[piedmont glacier]]s during the [[Quaternary glaciation]]s. The [[last glacial period]] is called [[Llanquihue glaciation]] in Chile after the terminal [[moraine]] systems around the lake.<ref>Patagonia Chilena {{ISBN|978-956-310-774-6}} {{Page needed|date=October 2010}}</ref>

Some historians consider Llanquihue Lake to have been within the range of ancient [[Chono people|Chono nomadism]].<ref name=medicos>{{Cite journal|title=Poblaciones costeras de Chile: marcadores genéticos en cuatro localidades|journal=[[Revista Médica de Chile|Revista médica de Chile]]|doi=10.4067/S0034-98871998000700002|url=https://scielo.conicyt.cl/scielo.php?pid=S0034-98871998000700002&script=sci_arttext#16.|year=1998|last3=Moreno S.|first3=Rodrigo|last4=Quiroz L.|first4=Daniel|volume=126 |issue=7 |doi-access=free}}</ref>

Llanquihue Lake is located in southern Chile a territory of northern Patagonia in the Los Lagos Region. The lake's views of [[Volcán Osorno]] make the surrounding cities such as [[Puerto Varas]] tourism hotspots.

